Atomic polarizabilities in a.u. (bohr^3) from fields of 0.005 a.u. (field sign of the input reversed)
alpha = alpha_p + alpha_c: alpha_p from the atom's own dipole, alpha_c from Keith's charge translation through the
bonds (bond charges weighted 1/rho at the bond point, as in PolaBer); tensors symmetrized.
frozen: partition weights and bond points of the zero-field density; moving: rebuilt for every field.

Bond graph (zero field): atoms, distance of the bond point from the first atom (bohr), rho there (a.u.)
